          "start": 7,
          "before": [],
          "after": [
            "",
            "- Classify normal connected Unix stream rows separately from the unique selected",
            "  listening inode in the QA host-topology controller. Reject malformed or unknown",
            "  selected-path rows and preserve descriptor/PID/namespace/identity checks.",
            "  An owned nonroot socket probe reproduces the parser bug; hosted descriptor",
            "  access remains independently blocked, and no runtime acceptance is implied.",
            "  Preserve all accepted proof seals through an exact outer source reversal."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "docs/ci-cd-strategy.md": {
      "baseline_raw_sha256": "c3cfd86861ab6e9c9eb9874b6d7f96ca757f3db18699d894889a61cb552ae7d0",
      "current_raw_sha256": "82596fd1933ba50ba422bf3588794f6fd11e29cac275471f600424e6b2686215",
      "hunks": [
        {
          "start": 28,
          "before": [],
          "after": [
            "",
            "### Selected Unix listener classification",
            "",
            "Exact-b5 PR-event run `36817024600` reported closed refusals:",
            "E2E job `110224240488` (`topology/daemon-descriptors-inaccessible`) and Contract",
            "job `110224240544` (`topology/ambiguous-selected-listener`). These witnesses do",
            "not expose private hosted rows or establish their contents.",
            "",
            "A separate owned, nonroot Linux socket probe (read-only, network-none; no daemon",
            "or site access) reproduced a parser assumption: one canonical pathname may have",
            "both a listening stream row (`Flags=00010000`, `Type=0001`, `St=01`) and a normal",
            "accepted connected stream row (`00000000`, `0001`, `03`). The controller now",
            "classifies only these two exact shapes, counting only listening inodes. It still",
            "requires exactly one listener, rejects malformed/unknown selected-path records,",
            "and preserves canonical alias/realpath, bounded reads, PID-hint socket-fd ownership,",
            "descriptor readlink/access, process identity/start time and namespace continuity.",
            "Synthetic differential tests show the old predicate rejects the normal pair;",
            "they do not prove this pair occurred in hosted Contract evidence.",
            "",
            "The independent descriptor-access refusal remains blocked. No privileges,",
            "runtime configuration, grants, custody, deadlines or workflow changes are part",
            "of this correction. Parser validation is not WordPress/daemon admission."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "scripts/untrusted-host-topology.php": {
      "baseline_raw_sha256": "acf569cce5b595e01d5f8208ec88159e511214f0697b97552ad0a79af9ed97aa",
      "current_raw_sha256": "2c0951d9097e3b9b8246e7247dabfd6034a5b50680bee7963827968f5866f3e8",
      "hunks": [
        {
          "start": 174,
          "before": [],
          "after": [
            "\t/** Classify only canonical-path rows; connected streams are not listening inodes. */",
            "\tpublic static function selected_listener( array $rows ): string {",
            "\t\t$listeners = array();",
            "\t\t$inodes = array();",
            "\t\tforeach ( $rows as $columns ) {",
            "\t\t\tself::require( is_array( $columns ) && array_keys( $columns ) === range( 0, 7 )",
            "\t\t\t\t&& count( array_filter( $columns, 'is_string' ) ) === 8",
            "\t\t\t\t&& 1 === preg_match( '/^(?:[0-9a-fA-F]{8}|[0-9a-fA-F]{16}):$/D', $columns[0] )",
            "\t\t\t\t&& 1 === preg_match( '/^[0-9a-fA-F]{8}$/D', $columns[1] ) && hexdec( $columns[1] ) > 0",
            "\t\t\t\t&& '00000000' === $columns[2] && '0001' === $columns[4]",
            "\t\t\t\t&& 1 === preg_match( '/^[1-9][0-9]{0,19}$/D', $columns[6] )",
            "\t\t\t\t&& ( strlen( $columns[6] ) < 20 || strcmp( $columns[6], '18446744073709551615' ) <= 0 )",
            "\t\t\t\t&& ! isset( $inodes[ $columns[6] ] )",
            "\t\t\t\t&& in_array( $columns[7], array( '/run/docker.sock', '/var/run/docker.sock' ), true )",
            "\t\t\t\t&& ( ( '00010000' === $columns[3] && '01' === $columns[5] )",
            "\t\t\t\t\t|| ( '00000000' === $columns[3] && '03' === $columns[5] ) ), 'ambiguous-selected-listener' );",
            "\t\t\t$inodes[ $columns[6] ] = true;",
            "\t\t\tif ( '00010000' === $columns[3] ) { $listeners[] = $columns[6]; }",
            "\t\t}",
            "\t\tself::require( 1 === count( $listeners ), 'selected-listener-not-unique' );",
            "\t\treturn $listeners[0];",
            "\t}",
            ""
          ]
        },
        {
          "start": 205,
          "before": [
            "\t\t$listener = array();"
          ],
          "after": [
            "\t\t$rows = array();"
          ]
        },
        {
          "start": 207,
          "before": [
            "\t\t\t$columns = preg_split( '/\\s+/', trim( $line ), 8 );",
            "\t\t\tif ( 8 !== count( $columns ) || ! in_array( $columns[7], array( '/run/docker.sock', '/var/run/docker.sock' ), true ) ) { continue; }",
            "\t\t\tif ( realpath( $columns[7] ) !== $socket ) { continue; }",
            "\t\t\tself::require( '00010000' === $columns[3] && '0001' === $columns[4] && '01' === $columns[5]",
            "\t\t\t\t&& ctype_digit( $columns[6] ), 'ambiguous-selected-listener' );",
            "\t\t\t$listener[] = $columns[6];"
          ],
          "after": [
            "\t\t\t$columns = preg_split( '/\\s+/', trim( $line ) );",
            "\t\t\t$aliases = array_intersect( array( '/run/docker.sock', '/var/run/docker.sock' ), $columns );",
            "\t\t\tif ( array() === $aliases || realpath( reset( $aliases ) ) !== $socket ) { continue; }",
            "\t\t\t$rows[] = $columns;"
          ]
        },
        {
          "start": 212,
          "before": [
            "\t\tself::require( 1 === count( $listener ), 'selected-listener-not-unique' );"
          ],
          "after": [
            "\t\t$listener = array( self::selected_listener( $rows ) );"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
